IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-gate`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-powers`

-- Tests for il-interpretation-powers.l4 (Law ss 11 to 19).
-- Expected values were decided from the words of each section before the module was run. A failing assertion is a
-- finding: none was edited to match the code. `a matter nothing displaces` and its two displaced siblings are defined in
-- il-interpretation-gate.l4.

§ `Tests: the interpretation of powers`

§§ `s 11: no time fixed`

`an authorisation with no time fixed` MEANS `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing` WITH
    `its kind` IS `an authorisation`
    `the enactment fixes a time for doing it` IS FALSE

`an obligation with no time fixed` MEANS `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing` WITH
    `its kind` IS `an obligation`
    `the enactment fixes a time for doing it` IS FALSE

`an obligation with a time fixed` MEANS `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing` WITH
    `its kind` IS `an obligation`
    `the enactment fixes a time for doing it` IS TRUE

`an authorisation with a time fixed` MEANS `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing` WITH
    `its kind` IS `an authorisation`
    `the enactment fixes a time for doing it` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 11 — what the authority amounts to when no time is fixed:` `an authorisation with no time fixed` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS `a power to do it with the proper speed, and again from time to time as the circumstances require`
#ASSERT `s 11 — what the authority amounts to when no time is fixed:` `an obligation with no time fixed` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS `a duty to do it with the proper speed, and again from time to time as the circumstances require`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11 — what the authority amounts to when no time is fixed:` `an obligation with a time fixed` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11 — what the authority amounts to when no time is fixed:` `an authorisation with a time fixed` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11 — what the authority amounts to when no time is fixed:` `an obligation with no time fixed` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

-- The proper speed, a judgement input, on both sides.
#ASSERT `s 11 — the thing was done in time:` `an obligation with no time fixed` `, the time taken being the proper speed:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 11 — the thing was done in time:` `an obligation with no time fixed` `, the time taken being the proper speed:` FALSE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 11 — the thing was done in time:` `an authorisation with no time fixed` `, the time taken being the proper speed:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11 — the thing was done in time:` `an obligation with a time fixed` `, the time taken being the proper speed:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11 — the thing was done in time:` `an obligation with no time fixed` `, the time taken being the proper speed:` TRUE `, for` `a matter whose context is inconsistent with the Law`
-- Again from time to time as the circumstances require.
#ASSERT `s 11 — it is to be done again:` `an obligation with no time fixed` `, the circumstances requiring it:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 11 — it is to be done again:` `an obligation with no time fixed` `, the circumstances requiring it:` FALSE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11 — it is to be done again:` `an authorisation with a time fixed` `, the circumstances requiring it:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed"

§§ `s 12: a power to give relief`

#ASSERT `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `an exemption` `in full` `without conditions` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `an exemption` `in part` `without conditions` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `an exemption` `in full` `on conditions` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `an exemption` `in part` `on conditions` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `a relief` `in part` `on conditions` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `a discount` `in part` `without conditions` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `something like an exemption, relief or discount` `in full` `on conditions` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `something else` `in part` `on conditions` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` `an exemption` `in part` `on conditions` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

§§ `s 13(a): appointing, authorising and charging, by name or by office`

#ASSERT `s 13(a) — the power to appoint, authorise or charge a person may be exercised` `appointing the person` `by naming the person` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 13(a) — the power to appoint, authorise or charge a person may be exercised` `appointing the person` `by naming the person's office` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 13(a) — the power to appoint, authorise or charge a person may be exercised` `authorising the person` `by naming the person's office` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 13(a) — the power to appoint, authorise or charge a person may be exercised` `imposing a duty on the person` `by naming the person` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 13(a) — the power to appoint, authorise or charge a person may be exercised` `imposing a duty on the person` `by naming the person's office` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(a) — the power to appoint, authorise or charge a person may be exercised` `appointing the person` `in some other way` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 13(a) — the power to appoint, authorise or charge a person may be exercised` `appointing the person` `by naming the person` `, for` `a matter whose context is inconsistent with the Law`

§§ `s 13(b): an appointment by the name of the office alone is of whoever fills the office`

`Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021` MEANS `A holder of an office` WITH `person` IS "Rivka", `from` IS YMD 2020 1 1, `until` IS YMD 2021 12 31
`Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023` MEANS `A holder of an office` WITH `person` IS "Dan", `from` IS YMD 2022 1 1, `until` IS YMD 2023 12 31
`Dan, office-holder from mid 2022` MEANS `A holder of an office` WITH `person` IS "Dan", `from` IS YMD 2022 6 1, `until` IS YMD 2023 12 31
`Rivka until mid 2022, overlapping Dan` MEANS `A holder of an office` WITH `person` IS "Rivka", `from` IS YMD 2020 1 1, `until` IS YMD 2022 6 30

#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2021 6 15) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Rivka"
-- Rivka's last day is "until" 2021-12-31, so (s 8) she is the holder on that day; Dan is from 2022-01-01.
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2021 12 31) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Rivka"
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2022 1 1) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Dan"
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2023 12 31) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Dan"
-- Before the first holder, after the last, and in a gap, the office has no holder and nobody is bound.
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2019 12 31) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2024 1 1) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2022 3 1) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder from mid 2022`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS NOTHING
-- ASSUMED, NOT RULED (fork F30): where two holders' terms overlap, the first listed is the holder.
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2022 6 15) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka until mid 2022, overlapping Dan`, `Dan, office-holder from mid 2022`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Rivka"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2021 6 15) `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`) `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

§§ `s 14: a power of appointment`

#ASSERT `s 14 — a power to make an appointment covers` `making the appointment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 14 — a power to make an appointment covers` `suspending its validity` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 14 — a power to make an appointment covers` `cancelling it` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 14 — a power to make an appointment covers` `dismissing the appointee` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 14 — a power to make an appointment covers` `suspending the appointee from the post` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 14 — a power to make an appointment covers` `something else` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 14 — a power to make an appointment covers` `cancelling it` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

§§ `s 15: a power to make regulations or give a direction`

`amending regulations in the way they were made` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH
    `what they are` IS `regulations`, `what is done to them` IS `amending them`, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS TRUE
`changing regulations in the way they were made` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH
    `what they are` IS `regulations`, `what is done to them` IS `changing them`, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS TRUE
`suspending regulations in the way they were made` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH
    `what they are` IS `regulations`, `what is done to them` IS `suspending them`, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS TRUE
`cancelling regulations in the way they were made` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH
    `what they are` IS `regulations`, `what is done to them` IS `cancelling them`, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS TRUE
`cancelling a direction in the way it was given` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH
    `what they are` IS `an administrative direction`, `what is done to them` IS `cancelling them`, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS TRUE
`cancelling regulations in some other way` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH
    `what they are` IS `regulations`, `what is done to them` IS `cancelling them`, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS FALSE
`cancelling something that is neither regulations nor a direction` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH
    `what they are` IS `something else`, `what is done to them` IS `cancelling them`, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS TRUE
`doing something else to regulations` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH
    `what they are` IS `regulations`, `what is done to them` IS `something else`, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `amending regulations in the way they were made` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `changing regulations in the way they were made` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `suspending regulations in the way they were made` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `cancelling regulations in the way they were made` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `cancelling a direction in the way it was given` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `cancelling regulations in some other way` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `cancelling something that is neither regulations nor a direction` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `doing something else to regulations` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` `cancelling regulations in the way they were made` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

