§§ `s 19: powers and duties under other enactments are kept`

#ASSERT NOT `s 19 — a grant of power or an imposition of duty, by itself, takes away from a power or duty under another enactment, something else doing so:` FALSE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 19 — a grant of power or an imposition of duty, by itself, takes away from a power or duty under another enactment, something else doing so:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 19 speaks only of the grant by itself; whether something else in an enactment takes away the other power or duty is for that enactment"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 19 — a grant of power or an imposition of duty, by itself, takes away from a power or duty under another enactment, something else doing so:` FALSE `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

§§ `s 13(b): a designation by the person's name alone, and by the name and the office`

-- tests: L13b
-- By the name alone the person named is bound, whoever fills the office; by the office alone it is the holder (as above);
-- by name and office together (b) says nothing, so the module refuses.
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2021 6 15) `by a designation that names` (`the person by name alone` "Moshe") `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Moshe"
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2022 6 15) `by a designation that names` (`the person by name alone` "Moshe") `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Moshe"
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2019 1 1) `by a designation that names` (`the person by name alone` "Moshe") `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Moshe"
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2021 6 15) `by a designation that names` `the office by name alone` `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Rivka"
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2022 6 15) `by a designation that names` `the office by name alone` `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS JUST "Dan"
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2019 12 31) `by a designation that names` `the office by name alone` `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2021 6 15) `by a designation that names` `the person by name and the office by name` `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 13(b) speaks of a designation by the name of the office alone; a designation by the person's name and the office's name is outside it, and neither it nor s 13(a) says whether such a designation binds the person named or whoever fills the office"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2021 6 15) `by a designation that names` (`the person by name alone` "Moshe") `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter another provision deals with` BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 13(b) — the person bound on` (YMD 2021 6 15) `by a designation that names` `the office by name alone` `, among the holders` (LIST `Rivka, office-holder 2020 and 2021`, `Dan, office-holder 2022 and 2023`) `, for` `a matter whose context is inconsistent with the Law` BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"

§§ `s 20: where the enactment requires all of the persons to act`

-- tests: L20
-- Where the enactment requires all to act, that is "another provision on the matter" (s 1): s 20 does not apply and the module refuses.
-- Where it does not, the answer is pass 1's.
#ASSERT `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 5 `persons was validly done when` 3
#ASSERT `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 3 `persons was validly done when` 2
#ASSERT `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 4 `persons was validly done when` 3
#ASSERT `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 1 `persons was validly done when` 1
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 5 `persons was validly done when` 2
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 4 `persons was validly done when` 2
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 2 `persons was validly done when` 1
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 1 `persons was validly done when` 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` TRUE `, an act imposed on` 5 `persons was validly done when` 3 BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` TRUE `, an act imposed on` 5 `persons was validly done when` 5 BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` TRUE `, an act imposed on` 5 `persons was validly done when` 4 BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` TRUE `, an act imposed on` 3 `persons was validly done when` 2 BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` TRUE `, an act imposed on` 2 `persons was validly done when` 1 BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
-- Numbers that do not fit an act done by some of the persons still refuse, with pass 1's message.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` FALSE `, an act imposed on` 3 `persons was validly done when` 5 BECAUSE "s 20 speaks of an act imposed on several persons and done by some of them; the numbers given do not fit that"

§§ `s 13(b) and s 20: whether the rule applies`

-- tests: L13b L20
-- (b)'s rule (whoever fills the office from time to time) applies to a designation that names the office alone, and to no other.
#ASSERT `s 13(b) — the rule that the office-holder from time to time is bound applies to a designation that names` `the office by name alone` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(b) — the rule that the office-holder from time to time is bound applies to a designation that names` (`the person by name alone` "Moshe") `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(b) — the rule that the office-holder from time to time is bound applies to a designation that names` `the person by name and the office by name` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 13(b) — the rule that the office-holder from time to time is bound applies to a designation that names` `the office by name alone` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with` BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
-- s 20's rule of the majority applies unless the enactment requires all of the persons to act (that is another provision on the matter, s 1).
#ASSERT `s 20 — the rule of the majority applies to an act imposed on several persons, the enactment's requirement that all act being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the rule of the majority applies to an act imposed on several persons, the enactment's requirement that all act being` TRUE
